        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Five to ten minutes at each end.</strong> Build from an easy
            walk to your session effort in small steps, and come back down the same way — incline
            first, then speed — until you can hold a conversation. Do drills on the floor, never on
            the moving belt.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If the floor feels like it is moving when you step off, hold the rail and stand still.
            If you feel faint, stop, step onto the side rails and sit down. The step-on and
            step-off basics are in our
            <a href="/how-to-use-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">how to use a treadmill</a>
            guide, and repeated dizziness is a question for a doctor.
          </p>
